{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967350-more-shows-like-firefly","id":967350,"title":"More shows like \"Firefly\"?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-11T09:06:10-07:00","id":967350,"title":"More shows like \"Firefly\"?","content":"I was recently rewatching Firefly because, why not? Now I find myself looking for something with a similar look and feel, and hopefully, at least half as entertaining!<br /> <br /> But there seems to be a surprising lack in the &quot;small band of misfit heroes traveling space in their smallish starship, trying to make ends meet while dealing with personal issues and overcoming dangerous obstacles&quot; genre, or maybe I just don't know where to look, so, any suggestions? About the only other one I can think of is Cowboy Bebop (yes, anime is acceptable, too!)...<br /> <br /> Apropos of little, some friends of mine where debating about a &quot;scale of importance/effectiveness&quot; in sci-fi shows, that ranges from casts of characters with little to no importance to the universe in the grand scheme of things (however cool and entertaining they might be anyway), such as the Serenity and Bebop crews, to characters who are THE movers and shakers of events on a galactic (or larger) scale, such as Star Wars and Babylon 5. Starfleet crews on the various Star Trek series fit somewhere in between, being highly trained, valuable personnel, who are nonetheless just doing their jobs, which *might* make a larger difference depending on the plot (as in DS9)...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:14:14-07:00","id":967357,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;The 4400&quot; is leagues better than &quot;Firefly&quot;. As I understand it, part of the reason &quot;Firefly&quot; didn't continue was because Summer Glau left the show to be on &quot;The 4400&quot;. She starts in season 2. And I just, all around, find it much more compelling. Probably because I find Whedon's writing sloppy and campy in most cases. But the characters are compelling, there's this incredible child character who's one of my favorite characters in anything. It's so good. Check it out. It's on Netflix, and season 1 is only six episodes.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;Black Mirror&quot; is an amazing sci-fi show. &quot;Terra Nova&quot; is another, same writers as &quot;The 4400&quot;. All of these are on Netflix. &quot;Black Mirror&quot; is only seven episodes total (Netflix is releasing six more in October), and &quot;Terra Nova&quot; is one season.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: these are not all western sci-fi shows, but they're all sci-fi, and great sci-fi. That's the best I can do, but I highly recommend all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:28:12-07:00","id":967363,"title":"","content":"You know, I'd just been thinking lately that sci-fi with space ships at all is remarkably rare, given it's what I imagine most people think when they think &quot;sci-fi,&quot; let alone the Traveller (Traveller is a great RPG for Firefly-style play, and there has been talk that Firefly was inspired by a Traveller campaign) sort of sci-fi.<br /> <br /> I'll be watching this thread with interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:11:14-07:00","id":967385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967350-more-shows-like-firefly#post967350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there seems to be a surprising lack in the &quot;small band of misfit heroes traveling space in their smallish starship, trying to make ends meet while dealing with personal issues and overcoming dangerous obstacles&quot; genre, or maybe I just don't know where to look, so, any suggestions? About the only other one I can think of is Cowboy Bebop (yes, anime is acceptable, too!)...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so disappointed to hear this.<br /> <br /> Watch <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farscape\" target=\"_blank\">Farscape</a>. Best space show in decades. There's also <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lexx\" target=\"_blank\">Lexx</a> which was fantastic and, if you can manage to find someplace where it's available and don't mind a really old show, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blake%27s_7\" target=\"_blank\">Blake's 7</a>.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine always talks about a show called the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killjoys_(TV_series)\" target=\"_blank\">Killjoys</a>, too. I couldn't get past the first episode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T21:55:59-07:00","id":967761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967350-more-shows-like-firefly?p=967385#post967385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm so disappointed to hear this.<br /> <br /> Watch <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farscape\" target=\"_blank\">Farscape</a>. Best space show in decades. There's also <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lexx\" target=\"_blank\">Lexx</a> which was fantastic and, if you can manage to find someplace where it's available and don't mind a really old show, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blake%27s_7\" target=\"_blank\">Blake's 7</a>.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine always talks about a show called the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killjoys_(TV_series)\" target=\"_blank\">Killjoys</a>, too. I couldn't get past the first episode.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bKilljoys gets pretty good. The setting is a LOT like Firefly; distant future, doesn't seem like they have FTL, most episodes happen on the same 4 planets. <i>Dark Matter</i> is also a about a ship with a very small crew; worth giving a look.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T16:57:03-07:00","id":968828,"title":"","content":"Sadly, there really aren't any shows like Firefly...least not really...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrg