=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T17:37:23-07:00","id":968853,"title":"","content":"I get six posts into a Firefly thread and nobody suggests Cowboy Bebop?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T18:28:47-07:00","id":968889,"title":"","content":"There's also Red Dwarf. Dated, but still more modern than Blake's 7. More of a straight comedy, it does have its dramatic moments.<br /> <br /> Andromeda was pretty good at points. If anime counts, Outlaw Star is a classic that's been completely overshadowed by Cowboy Bebop, which came out in the same year.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Gone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967350-more-shows-like-firefly?p=968829#post968829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh!! I totally Second Lexx and Farscape! Those were pretty awesome shows. Lexx can be pretty out there...but I always loved it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember staying up late to catch the first season back in the late 90s when they were just movies on TMC or something. They really got great as time went by. Yes, can be really out there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967350-more-shows-like-firefly?p=968853#post968853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get six posts into a Firefly thread and nobody suggests Cowboy Bebop?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hand-of-Omega mentioned it in their first post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-13-2016, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T04:26:45-07:00","id":969137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967350-more-shows-like-firefly?p=968889#post968889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember staying up late to catch the first season back in the late 90s when they were just movies on TMC or something. They really got great as time went by. Yes, can be really out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might have been on Showtime... But yea, &quot;season 1&quot; was like four 2 hour movies. Then it moved over to the Sci-Fi channel(back when that was channel was awesome).<br /> <br /> It was waaaay out there. But, if you kept up with it, it was totally worth watching it. The weirdness just sucks you in.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T04:33:25-07:00","id":969141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967350-more-shows-like-firefly?p=968889#post968889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(. . . ) If anime counts, Outlaw Star is a classic that's been completely overshadowed by Cowboy Bebop, which came out in the same year.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>love</i> <b>Outlaw Star</b> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=T_BTfScDlBA\" target=\"_blank\"><u>Toonami promo</u></a>). Its such a shame that no one's made anything else quite like it since. Only <i>one</i> episode was filler, and even it served to introduce a key plot point. Cyborgs, shapeshifting aliens, technomages . . .<br /> <br /> <b>Hand-of-Omega</b>? If you haven't seen it yet, I think <i>Outlaw Star</i> is exactly what you're looking for. Its got some psuedo-fantasy elements, but its still a great space opera. A mercenary/bounty hunter on a backwater frontier world stumbles into a plot to find a legendary treasure, with the clues scattered across the galaxy. He assembles a nicely eclectic crew, and the finale . . . wow. Uses a lot of &quot;Wild West&quot; story elements, such as gunslingers dueling over a woman, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T07:30:31-07:00","id":975040,"title":"","content":"Just finished Dark Matter on Netflix. Yes, yes, YES!! That's *exactly* what I was looking for, and can't wait to start S2! The crew all being amnesiac and rediscovering their pasts and relationships adds a new layer and, frankly, gives it a stronger narrative drive than Firefly, although Firefly definitely had better world-building. <br /> <br /> Will look into Farscape, as that's also on Netflix,and a friend has all of Outlaw Star on DVD, so I'll borrow that...Killjoys sounds interesting. All in all, great recommendations, guys, thanks!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T14:12:53-07:00","id":976093,"title":"","content":"There is nothing like 'Firefly'. But maybe 'The Expanse'? It's a good sci-fi TV show, at least, and they those aren't easy to find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12469-golconda","name":"Golconda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T12:19:48-07:00","id":978530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Golconda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967350-more-shows-like-firefly?p=976093#post976093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is nothing like 'Firefly'. But maybe 'The Expanse'? It's a good sci-fi TV show, at least, and they those aren't easy to find.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, The Expanse is a totally different sub-genre, but yeah, it's pretty awesome! Gotta say, SyFy is really coming back with some quality SF shows, from Childhood's End to Dark Matter and others...Now if only they'd go back to being &quot;Sci-Fi&quot;...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Personally, I'd love it if they made at least one miniseries a year, based on a classic SF book. My recommendation would be The Stars My Destination or Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep? I'd really love to see the latter, as Blade Runner only took about 30% of that book onscreen, there was *so much more* going on that would be fascinating to see visualized!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T12:37:27-07:00","id":979205,"title":"","content":"<i>Blake's 7</i> is kinda the original rebel misfits sci-fi series. It has a great ensemble and some quality long-term character development. The downside is that it's even lower-budget than the 80s <i>Doctor Who</i> it shared props and costumes with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:50:55-07:00","id":981630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967350-more-shows-like-firefly#post967350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was recently rewatching Firefly because, why not? Now I find myself looking for something with a similar look and feel, and hopefully, at least half as entertaining!<br /> <br /> But there seems to be a surprising lack in the &quot;small band of misfit heroes traveling space in their smallish starship, trying to make ends meet while dealing with personal issues and overcoming dangerous obstacles&quot; genre, or maybe I just don't know where to look, so, any suggestions? About the only other one I can think of is Cowboy Bebop (yes, anime is acceptable, too!)...<br /> <br /> Apropos of little, some friends of mine where debating about a &quot;scale of importance/effectiveness&quot; in sci-fi shows, that ranges from casts of characters with little to no importance to the universe in the grand scheme of things (however cool and entertaining they might be anyway), such as the Serenity and Bebop crews, to characters who are THE movers and shakers of events on a galactic (or larger) scale, such as Star Wars and Babylon 5. Starfleet crews on the various Star Trek series fit somewhere in between, being highly trained, valuable personnel, who are nonetheless just doing their jobs, which *might* make a larger difference depending on the plot (as in DS9)...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Outlaw Star. Outlaw Star. OUTLAW STAR.<br /> <br /> It kinda falls apart near the end, but it's fantastic in that narrow genre aside.<br /> <br /> ...yeah okay the grappling is a little silly, but it's still like, the premier anime about a small crew and ship doing underworld shit across an interesting universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T18:25:00-07:00","id":983058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967350-more-shows-like-firefly?p=968853#post968853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get six posts into a Firefly thread and nobody suggests Cowboy Bebop?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cowboy Bebop is life. But it was mentioned in the OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}